{"q":"224","t":"Basic Calculator","d":"Hard","p":false,"c":"<p>Given a string <code>s</code> representing a valid expression, implement a basic calculator to evaluate it, and return <em>the result of the evaluation</em>.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> You are <strong>not</strong> allowed to use any built-in function which evaluates strings as mathematical expressions, such as <code>eval()</code>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> s = &quot;1 + 1&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> s = &quot; 2-1 + 2 &quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> s = &quot;(1+(4+5+2)-3)+(6+8)&quot;\n<strong>Output:</strong> 23\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= s.length &lt;= 3 * 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>\n\t<li><code>s</code> consists of digits, <code>&#39;+&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;-&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;(&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;)&#39;</code>, and <code>&#39; &#39;</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>s</code> represents a valid expression.</li>\n\t<li><code>&#39;+&#39;</code> is <strong>not</strong> used as a unary operation (i.e., <code>&quot;+1&quot;</code> and <code>&quot;+(2 + 3)&quot;</code> is invalid).</li>\n\t<li><code>&#39;-&#39;</code> could be used as a unary operation (i.e., <code>&quot;-1&quot;</code> and <code>&quot;-(2 + 3)&quot;</code> is valid).</li>\n\t<li>There will be no two consecutive operators in the input.</li>\n\t<li>Every number and running calculation will fit in a signed 32-bit integer.</li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"calculate\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"s\",\r\n      \"type\": \"string\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Math","slug":"math"},{"name":"String","slug":"string"},{"name":"Stack","slug":"stack"},{"name":"Recursion","slug":"recursion"}],"s":[{"t":"Evaluate Reverse Polish Notation","s":"evaluate-reverse-polish-notation","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Basic Calculator II","s":"basic-calculator-ii","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Different Ways to Add Parentheses","s":"different-ways-to-add-parentheses","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Expression Add Operators","s":"expression-add-operators","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Basic Calculator III","s":"basic-calculator-iii","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"The Score of Students Solving Math Expression","s":"the-score-of-students-solving-math-expression","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Minimize Result by Adding Parentheses to Expression","s":"minimize-result-by-adding-parentheses-to-expression","d":"Medium","p":false}],"co":[["Microsoft","microsoft"],["Google","google"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Squarepoint Capital","squarepoint-capital"],["TikTok","tiktok"],["Boeing","boeing"],["Ericsson","ericsson"],["Meta","facebook"],["Uber","uber"],["Snowflake","snowflake"],["DoorDash","doordash"],["ByteDance","bytedance"],["Walmart Labs","walmart-labs"],["Ripple","ripple"],["Palo Alto Networks","palo-alto-networks"]]}